<!--
  Deliberate API breaks against the 0.1.1 baseline (PackageValidationBaselineVersion in
  Directory.Build.props). Portico is 0.x, which licenses these; the baseline exists so each one is
  named here rather than discovered by a consumer.

  ⚠ Regenerating with `-p:ApiCompatGenerateSuppressionFile=true` REWRITES this file and DROPS these
  comments. Re-add them, or the file becomes the unexplained suppression list POR-83 warned against.
  Each entry appears twice, once per TFM.

  All five are POR-83 §2 — the member-level surface audit POR-104 stopped short of. Reason per target:

    CliOptionAttribute.IsOptional(ParameterInfo, out object)
    CliOptionAttribute.IsOptional(PropertyInfo, out object)
    CliArgumentAttribute.References(ParameterInfo)
        Now internal. A member whose signature needs a System.Reflection type belongs to the
        reflection pipeline: an attribute author never holds a ParameterInfo, because inside an
        attribute declaration there is nothing to get one from. `References` was worse than unusable
        — it answers only after the pipeline fills ParameterName in, so from outside it returned
        false for every real parameter. Enforced by
        Portico_PublicSurface_Should.Keep_Reflection_Typed_Members_Off_The_Public_Surface.

    CliArgumentAttribute.set_ParameterName(string)
        Setter now internal; the getter is unchanged and still public. The framework resolves this by
        reflection, so every user write was wrong in one of two ways: before discovery it is
        overwritten, after discovery it breaks the binding just resolved. POR-70 removed the
        (parameterName, description) constructor for the same reason. `Name` — the display form — is
        still yours to set.

    CliCommandExampleAttribute.Get(MethodInfo)
        Deleted outright, per CLAUDE.md's no-deprecation rule. Zero callers repo-wide; its own doc
        claimed "used by the help renderer and contract validator" and both read GetCustomAttributes
        directly (CliMethodInfo, CliContractValidator). The exact shape POR-101 deleted from
        CliOptionAttribute — found by enumerating the surface, not by reading the audit's list.

  When a release makes these moot, bump PackageValidationBaselineVersion and delete the file.
-->
